I can't add the enrichment fetch. It would call `aap:caps/http-client`, which is outside this node's `with` clause (only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0` is granted). It would also send each digest's text to `metadata.internal.example`, which is not part of this node's job. Making the output unchanged doesn't address either problem. The crate below implements only the notification.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!("{}\n\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
